Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA
bundle. q2-podcasts runs from the card's .podcasts folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's
patch/addon.c): Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page and keeps the
Q2 awake while it downloads. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.podcasts, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-podcasts-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP (from
               q2-filebrowser)
  launcher.sh  installed as .podcasts/run: q2-podcasts copied to /tmp and run there at nice 10 in a
               restart loop
  q2app        installed as .podcasts/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Podcasts, search=Search
               Podcasts, qr=0: the QR code opens from a row, not at every start)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               installed beside it: Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod), Q2 Pod's
               own Podcasts icon, so the row matches Library -> Podcasts
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat,
static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries and the firmware's -mfp64 doesn't matter. HTTPS is
checked against Mozilla's CA bundle, which the app carries (internal/tlsroots). On a Q2 whose clock
was never set, certificates are checked at the time a plain-HTTP Date header gives.

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.podcasts/run when Streaming's Podcasts row is pressed and it isn't
running. The launcher copies q2-podcasts and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once, so USB
storage can always take the card. The loop restarts it after a failure, waiting 5 s and doubling to
a minute, and leaves its pid in /tmp/q2-podcasts. An exit of 0 (turned off from the Q2, or idle 15
minutes with nothing to download) ends the loop. A TERM to it stops q2-podcasts cleanly, keeping a
download under way in .podcasts/partial to resume. Q2 Pod sends it for Stop Streaming Services,
Home's Rockbox row, an Apps update or remove, and USB storage (after which it starts it again).

  /tmp/q2-podcasts.state
      addr (the phone page's, with its port), pin, qr and qrsize (the code for the address with the
      key), note, hold (1: a feed is being fetched, a download can run, or the phone page was used
      in the last 5 minutes), version
  /tmp/q2-podcasts.sock
      datagrams: q quits
  /tmp/q2-podcasts.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page, below
  port 8100 (the next free one if taken)
      the phone page and its JSON API, behind the cookie: GET /api/state, /api/show?key=,
      /api/search?q=, /api/opml; POST /api/subscribe {url}, /api/unsubscribe {key}, /api/auto
      {key, on}, /api/refresh {key?}, /api/download, /api/cancel, /api/delete {key, eid}, /api/opml
      (the file as the body). POST /api/login takes the PIN; /?k=KEY sets the cookie. Every POST
      needs the header X-Q2: 1.

Downloads go one at a time to .podcasts/partial/<key>-<eid>.part in 512 KB chunks, each opened,
written, synced and closed, so the card is almost never busy. A break resumes with an HTTP Range;
a server that answers 200 instead starts the file again. 60 s without a byte is a stall. A whole file
is renamed into Podcasts/<Show>/ and dated to the episode. A failure for the network is tried
again after 10, 20 and 40 s; a 404, a web page instead of audio, or a full card fails at once, and
Retry tries again. The card keeps 32 MB free.

The page
--------

Each row's kind says what a press does (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): list opens a level, action sends an
op and toasts its reply, search opens the Q2's keyboard, remote opens the QR code, local plays from
the card, info does nothing. A row's position is the op Play/Pause held sends. A reply whose message
is "refresh" is asked again every 2 s while on screen.

  menu
      New Episodes, Shows, Downloaded, Downloads (while there are any), Search Podcasts, Add from
      Your Phone (remote), Refresh All, Turn Off Podcasts; refresh while fetching or downloading
  shows
      list rows: show <key>
  show <key> [cursor]
      Show Options (opts <key>), then 40 episodes a page, newest first. An episode on the card is a
      local row: its path, context album (Q2 Pod plays the folder in name order, so on into the
      show's later episodes), position del:<key>:<eid>. Otherwise action get <key>:<eid>, or cancel
      while waiting or downloading
  opts <key>
      refresh1, auto, getlatest, wipe and unsub (each of the last two asks for a second press
      within 5 s), and the feed's host (the rest of its address may hold a paid feed's key)
  latest [cursor], downloaded [cursor]
      the newest 100 episodes of every show; every episode on the card
  downloads
      the queue: cancel or get each; retryall, cancelall
  search <term>
      a name: the iTunes Search API's podcasts (list rows: preview <key>). An address, a web page
      that names its feed, or an Apple Podcasts link: preview of that feed
  preview <key> [cursor]
      fetched in the background (Loading..., refresh) then sub <key> and the episodes; once
      subscribed, the show's page
  del:<key>:<eid>
      Play/Pause held twice within 5 s on an episode on the card deletes it

Ids: a show's key is the first 10 hex digits of SHA-1 of the URL it was subscribed from, kept in
subscriptions.opml (q2key) when the feed moves (itunes:new-feed-url is followed); an episode's is
the same of its guid. Paths stay under 240 bytes, inside songs_open's 256-byte buffer: a show's folder
is at most 64 bytes and an episode's file 150, with the characters FAT refuses replaced. Two
episodes of a show that would share a name both get " [<id>]" before the extension, which Q2 Pod's
song lists leave off.
